{"source_passage_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0003-PASSAGE", "text": "Basic Concepts of Cellular Energetics and Metabolism\n• Cellular Energetics\n• Processes that a cell obtains, transforms, applies energy.\n• These may include:\n• Exergonic chemical reactions that release energy\n• And endergonic chemical reactions that consume energy\n• All these reactions are collectively known as metabolism\n• Metabolism\n• Sum total of all biochemical reactions occuring in cell", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "source_file": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0003"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0003", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "source_file": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf", "page_number": 3, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 3, "pdf_page": 3, "formatted": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf, slide 3 (PDF p. 3)"}], "slide_number": 3, "section_ids": ["HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0003", "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-PART01", "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "HHS3190M-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS3190M - Human Physiology and Functional Anatomy for Rehabilitation Services", "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "Basic concepts of cellular energetics and metabolism", "Basic Concepts of Cellular Energetics and Metabolism"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
{"source_passage_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0004-PASSAGE", "text": "Basic Concepts of Cellular Energetics and Metabolism\n• Metabolic reactions are divided into\n• Anabolism\n• Reactions that use smaller molecules to build larger molecule. E.g. using amino acids to make protein\n• Cellular energy is used in these processes.\n• Catabolism\n• Reactions that break down complex molecules to simple molecules\n• Cellular energy is produced in these processes.\n• Cellular respiration is a group of catabolic reactions that food fuels (E.g. glucose) are broken down to produce cellular energy", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "source_file": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0004"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0004", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "source_file": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf", "page_number": 4, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 4, "pdf_page": 4, "formatted": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf, slide 4 (PDF p. 4)"}], "slide_number": 4, "section_ids": ["HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0004", "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-PART01", "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "HHS3190M-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS3190M - Human Physiology and Functional Anatomy for Rehabilitation Services", "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "Basic concepts of cellular energetics and metabolism", "Basic Concepts of Cellular Energetics and Metabolism"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
