{"source_passage_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0007-PASSAGE", "text": "Nature and Functions of Enzymes\n• Most cellular reactions are organic reactions that occur slowly without catalysts. Therefore, there are many enzymes in human body to control rates of different reactions.\n• Enzyme\n• Chemical nature: Specific sub-class of protein\n• Active site: Special 3-dimension conformation for binding of specific molecule\n• Function: Catalyze chemical reactions of specific molecule\n• Charactersitic: Do not change after the reaction", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "source_file": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0007"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0007", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "source_file": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf", "page_number": 7, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 7, "pdf_page": 7, "formatted": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf, slide 7 (PDF p. 7)"}], "slide_number": 7, "section_ids": ["HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0007", "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-PART02", "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "HHS3190M-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS3190M - Human Physiology and Functional Anatomy for Rehabilitation Services", "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "Nature and functions of enzymes", "Nature and Functions of Enzymes"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
