{"source_passage_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0013-PASSAGE", "text": "Nature and Functions of Enzymes\n• Factors that affect enzyme activity\n• (1) Temperature\n• When temperature is low, enzymes are inactive. Low enzyme activity leads to low reaction rate. When temperature increases, higher enzyme activity leads to higher reaction rate.\n• Maximal reaction rate is reached when temperature increases to optimum temperature (37-40˚C for most human enzymes).\n• When temperature increases furtherly, enzyme molecules are denatured to decrease enzyme activities. Reaction rate drops dramatically.", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "source_file": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0013"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0013", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "source_file": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf", "page_number": 13, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 13, "pdf_page": 13, "formatted": "07 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L4 (Jul 2026).pdf, slide 13 (PDF p. 13)"}], "slide_number": 13, "section_ids": ["HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0013", "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-PART02", "HHS3190M-L04-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "HHS3190M-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS3190M - Human Physiology and Functional Anatomy for Rehabilitation Services", "Lecture 4 - Cellular Energetics and Homeostasis (July 2026)", "Nature and functions of enzymes", "Nature and Functions of Enzymes"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
